[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Low-Level Requirements
UID: LLR-DOC
VERSION: 1.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-001
TITLE: Clap Derive Macro for CLI
STATEMENT: The system shall use clap's derive macro to define CLI argument structure.
RATIONALE: Derive macro provides type-safe and maintainable CLI definition.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-002
TITLE: Container Argument Structure
STATEMENT: The --container argument shall accept exactly three values: schema path, template path, and data path.
RATIONALE: Fixed argument count ensures all required inputs are provided.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-003
TITLE: Test Case Argument Structure
STATEMENT: The --test-case argument shall accept a verification methods directory followed by one or more test case files.
RATIONALE: Directory path enables dynamic schema/template lookup, and multiple files allow batch processing.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-004
TITLE: Exit Code 0 for Success
STATEMENT: The system shall return exit code 0 when processing completes successfully.
RATIONALE: Exit code 0 is the standard Unix convention for success.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-005
TITLE: Exit Code 1 for Usage Errors
STATEMENT: The system shall return exit code 1 for missing or invalid command-line arguments.
RATIONALE: Distinguishes user errors from system errors.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-006
TITLE: Exit Code 2 for File Errors
STATEMENT: The system shall return exit code 2 when required files are not found.
RATIONALE: File system errors should be distinguished from validation errors.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-007
TITLE: Exit Code 3 for Validation Errors
STATEMENT: The system shall return exit code 3 when schema validation fails.
RATIONALE: Validation errors indicate data quality issues requiring user attention.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-008
TITLE: JSONSchema Crate
STATEMENT: The system shall use the jsonschema crate for JSON Schema validation.
RATIONALE: jsonschema crate provides comprehensive JSON Schema specification support.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-009
TITLE: Validation Before Rendering
STATEMENT: The system shall validate all data files against their schemas before beginning template rendering.
RATIONALE: Early validation prevents wasted processing on invalid data.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-010
TITLE: Type Field Lookup
STATEMENT: The system shall read the 'type' field from each test case YAML file to determine the verification method.
RATIONALE: Type field enables dynamic schema and template selection.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-011
TITLE: Verification Method Directory Structure
STATEMENT: The system shall expect verification method directories to contain 'schema.json' and 'template.j2' or 'template.adoc' files.
RATIONALE: Standard naming convention simplifies file lookup logic.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-012
TITLE: Test Case Rendering Order
STATEMENT: The system shall render test cases in the order they are specified on the command line.
RATIONALE: Preserves user-specified ordering in the output documentation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-013
TITLE: Rendered Test Cases Variable
STATEMENT: The system shall provide rendered test cases to the container template as 'test_cases_md' or 'test_cases_adoc' variable.
RATIONALE: Variable naming indicates the content format and purpose.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-014
TITLE: Strip Filter Implementation
STATEMENT: The system shall implement a 'strip' filter that removes leading and trailing whitespace.
RATIONALE: Common operation for cleaning YAML data values.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-015
TITLE: Replace Filter Implementation
STATEMENT: The system shall implement a 'replace' filter that replaces substring occurrences with support for 'old', 'new', and optional 'times' parameters.
RATIONALE: Enables simple text substitution in templates.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-016
TITLE: Replace Regex Filter Implementation
STATEMENT: The system shall implement a 'replace_regex' filter that replaces regex pattern matches with support for 'old', 'new', and optional 'times' parameters.
RATIONALE: Enables advanced pattern-based text transformations.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-017
TITLE: Tera Context Population
STATEMENT: The system shall populate the Tera context with all fields from YAML data files as top-level variables.
RATIONALE: Direct field access simplifies template syntax.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-018
TITLE: Output File Writing
STATEMENT: The system shall write rendered output to the file specified by --output argument, or stdout if not specified.
RATIONALE: Flexibility in output destination supports both file generation and piping.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-019
TITLE: Template Extension Selection
STATEMENT: The system shall select templates with '.j2' extension for markdown format and '.adoc' extension for asciidoc format.
RATIONALE: File extension indicates template content type and syntax.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-020
TITLE: Requirements Summary Template
STATEMENT: The system shall optionally render a requirements_aggregation_template file if present in the verification methods directory.
RATIONALE: Provides consolidated requirements coverage view.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-021
TITLE: YAML Deserialization
STATEMENT: The system shall use serde_yaml to deserialize YAML data files into serde_json::Value objects.
RATIONALE: Unified Value representation simplifies template context handling.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-022
TITLE: Error Message Formatting
STATEMENT: The system shall provide descriptive error messages including file paths and validation details.
RATIONALE: Clear error messages improve debugging and user experience.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-023
TITLE: Temporary File for Test Cases
STATEMENT: The system shall write rendered test cases to a temporary file and provide its path to the container template.
RATIONALE: Allows container template to reference test cases content multiple times if needed.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-024
TITLE: Format Argument Validation
STATEMENT: The system shall accept only 'markdown' or 'asciidoc' as valid values for the --format argument.
RATIONALE: Restricts to supported output formats.
